From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] chassis: keep the boot type when the BIOS clears the boot flags
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for AMI BIOS behaviour]

The AMI BIOS on this board retires a one-time boot override by writing Set
System Boot Options parameter 5 with every bit zero. Bit 5 of data byte 1 is
the BIOS boot type, so that write also reads as "PC compatible (legacy)", and
the handler stored BootType=Legacy after every one-time boot.

Clients that set an override without BootSourceOverrideMode then inherit
Legacy: webui-vue never sends the mode, nor did bmclib's minimal-fields
fallback after bmcweb rejected its full Boot object. This board's boot order
is UEFI-only (BIOS boot option filter "UEFI only"), so a legacy PXE request
has no boot entry and the host quietly boots the disk instead.

A write that clears the valid bit revokes the override; it says nothing about
which mode the next override should use. Only apply the boot type from a
write that sets the valid bit.

--- a/chassishandler.cpp
+++ b/chassishandler.cpp
@@ -2315,7 +2315,17 @@
                 }
             }
 
-            if (typeIpmiToDbus.end() != typeItr)
+            // Only take the BIOS boot type from a write that sets the valid
+            // bit. The AMI BIOS retires a one-time override with an all-zero
+            // parameter 5, whose bit 5 reads as "PC compatible (legacy)";
+            // applying it rewrote BootType to Legacy after every one-time
+            // boot. Any client that then sets an override without a mode --
+            // webui-vue never sends BootSourceOverrideMode -- inherited
+            // Legacy, and on this UEFI-only boot order a legacy PXE request
+            // has no boot entry, so the host silently booted the disk. A
+            // clear revokes the override; it says nothing about the mode the
+            // next one should use.
+            if (validFlag && typeIpmiToDbus.end() != typeItr)
             {
                 rc = setBootType(ctx, typeItr->second);
                 if (rc != ipmi::ccSuccess)
